An expired enrollment code was presented for redemption. It was refused, and
no certificate was issued.

Two things cause this, and they need opposite responses:

  - A job you still want is failing. It has been renewing through this code,
    the code expired, and every renewal since has failed. Re-enroll it.

  - A credential you thought was gone is still in circulation. Nothing you
    run should be presenting a code that expired. If the address below is not
    a host you recognize, treat the code as leaked and audit what it was used
    for while it was still live.

ATTEMPT

  Attempted at          {{ datetime .AttemptedAt }}
  From address          {{ .SourceIP }}
  Code expired          {{ datetime .CodeExpiredAt }}

ENROLLMENT

  Service account       {{ .ServiceAccount }}
  Enrollment ID         {{ .EnrollmentID }}
{{ if .RequestID }}  Request ID            {{ .RequestID }}
{{ end }}  Key ID                {{ .KeyID }}
  Principals            {{ join .Principals ", " }}
  Enrolled key          {{ .PublicKeyType }} {{ .PublicKeyFingerprint }}

The caller was told only that the code is unknown -- an expired code and a
code that never existed answer identically, so whoever holds it learns nothing
from the refusal.

You will not get another message about this enrollment for a while, however
often the attempt repeats.
